      "summary": "This meta-analysis combined 53 studies of instruction for elementary pupils with or at risk for word-reading difficulties. Studies were conducted between 1980 and 2020 and included 6053 students. The authors found an overall positive effect on norm-referenced reading outcomes. Higher instructional dosage was associated with larger effects, while comprehension outcomes showed smaller effects than word-reading and spelling outcomes. The dosage relationship is an association across studies, not an individually tested prescription for app minutes. The review supports focused reading instruction and the need to distinguish word reading from understanding. Parents and teachers can use short games to revisit taught material, but should also look for reading in new examples and real text. Completing familiar picture-choice tasks does not establish the same outcomes measured in this review.",
