      "summary": "This meta-analysis evaluated 36 randomised trials of computerised cognitive training for people with ADHD. Working-memory performance improved, but improvements did not consistently extend to other cognitive tasks or academic outcomes. Probably blinded ratings showed no overall benefit for total ADHD symptoms or hyperactivity/impulsivity. A small benefit for inattention appeared partly specific to the setting where training took place. Some longer-term findings were promising, but involved relatively few trials. The practical message is to distinguish improvement on a practised mental task from wider changes in school functioning or reading. Games may provide enjoyable supported practice, but attention-game performance should not be presented as treatment progress. Reading difficulties still need direct assessment and teaching of reading skills, and individual supports should remain available.",
