      "summary": "This meta-analysis asked how word reading and oral language relate to reading comprehension in autistic children. It combined 26 studies of learners aged 6–18 and found substantial relationships between comprehension and both component skills. Their average relationships were similar in size. This challenges the assumption that an autistic child who struggles to understand text necessarily has intact word reading and only needs language work. Both areas should be considered when choosing support. Because these results concern associations, they do not show that practising any one game will cause a matching increase in comprehension. A parent or teacher can use separate observations of decoding and message understanding to identify questions for assessment, while maintaining communication supports and avoiding a single profile assumption for every autistic learner.",
