      "summary": "This systematic review examined cognitive training intended to improve executive functions and wider outcomes in children and adolescents with ADHD. It included 22 studies published in the searched period. Many reported gains on executive-function tasks, and some reported changes in symptoms, academic work or other behaviours; other studies did not find gains. The authors described cognitive training as a potentially complementary approach. This review's positive overall interpretation should be read alongside newer meta-analyses that distinguish blinded ratings and objective academic outcomes. Counting how many studies found a benefit is not the same as estimating a pooled reliable effect. Parents and teachers should ask whether gains extend beyond the practised task and whether direct support for learning difficulties is also being provided. No finding here validates our app's focus games.",
