      "summary": "This trial examined a parent-implemented dialogic-reading approach called RECALL for autistic preschoolers. Thirty-one children were allocated to treatment or control conditions. Following six weeks, the intervention group showed improvements in story comprehension, emotion knowledge and reading engagement. The authors suggested that structured prompting during shared reading may help some children obtain greater benefit from the interaction. These findings concern an adult-mediated reading approach, not simply exposure to illustrated stories. Parents and teachers should provide meaningful opportunities to respond through the child's available communication methods and supply help when needed. The small study does not establish the best approach for every autistic child, and the abstract does not fully describe longer-term generalisation or implementation demands. Our comic and story activities were not evaluated in this trial.",
